#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:5
msgid "Booting Linux on ZTE zx297520v3 SoCs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:7
msgid "Author: Stefan Dösinger"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:9
msgid "Date  : 27 Jan 2026"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:12
msgid "1. Hardware description"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:13
msgid ""
"Zx297520v3 SoCs use a 64-bit capable Cortex-A53 CPU and GICv3, although they "
"run in arm32 mode only. The CPU has support EL3, but no hypervisor (EL2) and "
"it seems to lack VFP and NEON."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:17
msgid ""
"The SoC is used in a number of cheap LTE to WiFi routers, both battery "
"powered MiFis and stationary CPEs. In addition to the CPU these devices "
"usually have 64 MB Ram (although some is shared with the LTE chip), 128 MB "
"NAND flash, an SDIO connected RTL8192-type Wifi chip limited to 2.4 ghz "
"operation, USB 2, and buttons. Devices with as low as 32 MB or as high as "
"128 MB ram exist, as do devices with 8 or 16 MB of NOR flash."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:24
msgid ""
"Some devices, especially the stationary ones, have 100 mbit Ethernet and an "
"Ethernet switch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:27
msgid ""
"Usually the devices have LEDs for status indication, although some have SPI "
"or I2C connected displays."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:30
msgid ""
"Some have an SD card slot. If it exists, it is a better choice for the root "
"file system because it easily outperforms the built-in NAND."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:33
msgid ""
"The LTE interface runs on a separate DSP called ZSP880. It is probably "
"derived from LSI ZSPs and has an undocumented instruction set. The ZSP "
"communicates with the main CPU via SRAM and DRAM and a mailbox hardware that "
"can generate IRQs on either ends."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:38
msgid ""
"There is also a Cortex M0 CPU, which is responsible for early HW "
"initialization and starting the Cortex A53 CPU. It does not have any "
"essential purpose once U-Boot is started. An SRAM-based handover protocol "
"exists to run custom code on this CPU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:44
msgid "2. Booting via USB"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:46
msgid ""
"The Boot ROM has support for booting custom code via USB. This mode can be "
"entered by connecting a Boot PIN to GND or by modifying the third byte on "
"NAND (set it to anything other than 0x5A aka 'Z'). A free software tool to "
"start custom U-Boot and kernels can be found here:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:51
msgid "https://github.com/zx297520v3-mainline/zx297520v3-loader"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:53
msgid ""
"If USB download mode is entered but no boot commands are sent through USB, "
"the device will proceed to boot normally after a few seconds. It is "
"therefore possible to enable USB boot permanently and still leave the "
"default boot files in place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:58
msgid "https://github.com/zx297520v3-mainline/u-boot-mainline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:60
msgid ""
"Contains an U-Boot version that can be used with the USB loader and sets up "
"the CPU and interrupt controller to comply with Linux's booting requirements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:64
msgid "3. Building for built-in U-Boot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:65
msgid ""
"The devices come with an ancient U-Boot that loads legacy uImages from NAND "
"and boots them without a chance for the user to interrupt. The images are "
"stored in files ap_cpuap.bin and ap_recovery.bin on a jffs2 partition named "
"imagefs, usually mtd4. A file named \"fotaflag\" switches between the two "
"modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:70
msgid ""
"In addition to the uImage header, those files have a 384-byte signature "
"header, which is used for authenticating the images on some devices. Most "
"devices have this authentication disabled and it is enough to pad the uImage "
"files with 384 zero bytes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:75
msgid ""
"Builtin U-Boot also poorly sets up the CPU. Read the next section for "
"details on this. It has no support for loading DTBs, so "
"CONFIG_ARM_APPENDED_DTB is needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:79
msgid ""
"So to build an image that boots from NAND the following steps are necessary:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:81
msgid "Patch the assembly code from section 3 into arch/arm/kernel/head.S."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:82
msgid "make zx29_defconfig"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:83
msgid "make [-j x]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:84
msgid ""
"cat arch/arm/boot/zImage arch/arm/boot/dts/zte/[device].dtb > kernel+dtb"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:85
msgid ""
"mkimage -A arm -O linux -T kernel -C none -a 0x20008000 -d kernel+dtb uimg"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:86
msgid "dd if=/dev/zero bs=1 count=384 of=ap_recovery.bin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:87
msgid "cat uimg >> ap_recovery.bin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:88
msgid ""
"Place this file onto imagefs on the device. Delete ap_cpuap.bin if the free "
"space is not enough."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:90
msgid "Create the file fotaflag: echo -n FOTA-RECOVERY > fotaflag"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:92
msgid ""
"For development, booting ap_recovery.bin is recommended because the normal "
"boot mode arms the watchdog before starting the kernel."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:96
msgid "4. CPU and GIC Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:98
msgid ""
"Generally CPU and GICv3 need to be set up according to the requirements "
"spelled out in Documentation/arch/arm64/booting.rst. For zx297520v3 this "
"means:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:101
msgid "GICD_CTLR.DS=1 to disable GIC security"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:102
msgid "Enable access to ICC_SRE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:103
msgid "Disable trapping IRQs into monitor mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:104
msgid "Configure EL2 and below to run in insecure mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:105
msgid "Configure timer PPIs to active-low."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../arch/arm/zte/zx297520v3.rst:107
msgid ""
"The kernel sources provided by ZTE do not boot either (interrupts do not "
"work at all). They are incomplete in other aspects too, so it is assumed "
"that there is some workaround similar to the one described in this document "
"somewhere in the binary blobs."
msgstr ""

